ion for AquaMaster4 FEW45Y.Z variant.\"\n\nFootnote on this table: marker \"[1]\". Add to table footnotes AND global footnotes.\n\nShould model_level also include software-related? No — keep in matrix_tables.\n\nAlso — the ratio note: \"Values Q3 and ratio Q3/Q1 are selected from paragraph 4.1 of OIML R49-1:2013\" — could cite in description. Yes included.\n\nThe number of models: 15 sizes. Also, is it right to omit per-combo models? I'll note in matrix description that class and power supply further subdivide variants. OK.\n\nOne more: type_designations — \"AquaMaster4 FEW45Y.Z\" — the fragment only names FEW45Y.Z as a variant. I'll include \"FEW45Y.Z\". Some might argue AquaMaster4 is the type name. family_name captures AquaMaster4.\n\nAlso certificate.scheme: \"A\" from \"R49/2013-A-NL1-20.01\". Yes.\n\nLet me also double check \"page_total\": headers say \"Page 5 of 13\", \"Page 6 of 13\", \"Page 7 of 13\" → total 13.\n\nWrite final JSON now. Keep it compact-ish. I'll include column_units only where relevant.\n\nAlso the \"-\" remarks: schema rule 8: empty strings are not values — use null. I'll use null.\n\nAlso for footnote_markers on table 4 title — attach to the matrix_tables entry via footnotes list, and global footnotes. In table's rows there's no per-value footnote; the footnote applies to the whole table. I'll add \"footnote_markers\": [\"[1]\"]? Schema matrix_tables doesn't have footnote_markers field, but has footnotes[]. I'll put footnote definition in both the table's footnotes and the global footnotes array. Hmm, duplication. Global footnotes[] is required by schema for footnote definitions; the table-level footnotes field can list markers. I'll set table \"footnotes\": [\"[1]\"] and global footnotes with definition. Actually to keep it simple, put definition once in global footnotes; table entry just references via its footnotes list with the marker. That seems reasonable.\n\nFinal JSON assembly. Ensure no LaTeX, snake_case labels, decimals with dots.\n\nAlso \"project_number\": \"3939609\" — keep as string (it's an identifier). \n\nrecommendation.accuracy_classes: [1, 2].\n\nLet me write it out.",
